<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The start chooser's own panel, floating over the live viewport.

  A Tier 2 context surface at the sheet radius, with the two options RECESSED
  into it rather than outlined on it. A panel and its options on neighbouring
  tones was one flat block: the options have to be the thing you reach for, and
  a well is the tonal way to say "this is a slot you choose".

  Borderless and raised. The outline it used to draw was most of what made this
  read as a settings dialog; a panel separated by tone and depth belongs to the
  same workspace as the viewport rendering behind it.

  A 1 dp HAIRLINE (`UI-CRAFT-R1`). Tone and a soft shadow alone left a
  translucent surface over a rendered model reading as a smudge rather than
  as an edge; the hairline, in the palette's own fsChromeHairline, is what
  every precision tool draws around a floating panel and is what makes the
  surface's corner crisp. It is a hairline and never a frame: 1 dp, at the
  low contrast the role was approved at.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="?attr/fsSurfaceContext" />
    <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_sheet" />
    <stroke
        android:width="@dimen/control_border_width"
        android:color="?attr/fsChromeHairline" />
</shape>
